## Do NOT

- Redesign the screen
- Simplify the layout without reason
- Change the component hierarchy
- Replace the design with a generic dashboard template
- Invent different colors
- Change spacing dramatically
- Move major sections
- Remove visible functionality
- Turn the reference into one large background image

## DO

- Recreate the interface using React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS
- Use real HTML/UI components
- Make buttons, forms, tables, and charts functional/dynamic
- Connect data to Supabase (or demo data until Supabase is configured)
- Preserve the reference’s visual hierarchy, approximate dimensions/spacing, card placement, typography hierarchy, border radius, and shadow style
- Make the implementation responsive

## Priority

The screenshot determines **HOW the page should look**.  
The system requirements determine **HOW the page should work**.  
Do not sacrifice one for the other.

## Workflow (every screen)

1. Open the matching file in `reference/ui/`
2. Study layout, navigation, cards, tables, forms, spacing, typography, colors, buttons, charts, filters, tabs, drawers/modals
3. Implement component-by-component to match
4. Compare against the reference before moving on
